  "scope": "47 of 69 numbered manuscript assertions remain completely verified; 22, including the main theorem, remain incomplete. This continuation completes the one-core branch of Corollary 4.6 from its original regular non-overfull multigraph hypotheses with at most three exceptional vertices. It constructs the actual complement coloring, normalizes core parity, and partitions all original copies into k perfect matchings with every uniform parameter before the host. It also factors terminal one-core pieces with bounded exterior and an unrestricted possible apex under the proved incidence hypotheses, and proves an exact safe circuit-deletion criterion on at most three labels. The two-core branch of 4.6, full fixed-pattern Lemma 4.4, general compatible-circuit selection, terminal Proposition 4.16, general Section 6 factorization, critical average-degree input, and the main theorem remain incomplete. Full Lemmas 4.2 and 4.14 and all historical completed assertions, declarations, and source-recovery mappings are preserved. No additional numbered assertion is claimed.",
